-- THE QUESTIONS OF NUMBERS KEEP
--
-- Every question the keep can ask, and the rule behind it. Kept in its own file so that the game
-- and the checker beside it ask exactly the same things.
--
-- Only three words are offered out. The makers below them are nobody else's business.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The rules worth remembering
--
-- Each one is a list of three pieces of text: its name, the rule itself, and the Hebrew for it.
-- They are written out once, here, and referred to everywhere else.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

please define the rule named with a which:
    remember out is an empty list

    check if which is 1:
        add "DIFFERENCE OF TWO SQUARES" to out
        add "(a + b)(a - b) = a squared - b squared" to out
        add "הפרש ריבועים" to out
    otherwise if which is 2:
        add "A SQUARE OPENED UP" to out
        add "(a + b) squared = a squared + 2ab + b squared" to out
        add "טרינום ריבועי" to out
    otherwise if which is 3:
        add "THE BOTTOM IS NEVER ZERO" to out
        add "set every bottom to 0 and solve. Those values of x are out of bounds." to out
        add "תחום הצבה" to out
    otherwise if which is 4:
        add "MINUS B OVER TWO A" to out
        add "the x of the vertex is -b divided by 2a. Put it back in to get the y." to out
        add "קדקוד הפרבולה" to out
    otherwise if which is 5:
        add "MAKE Y NOTHING" to out
        add "the zeros are where y = 0. Factor, and read each bracket." to out
        add "נקודות האפס" to out
    otherwise if which is 6:
        add "PUT X TO NOTHING" to out
        add "the y axis is where x = 0, so the answer is the number on its own." to out
        add "נקודת חיתוך עם ציר Y" to out
    otherwise if which is 7:
        add "A SMILES, MINUS A FROWNS" to out
        add "a above zero opens upward and has a lowest point. Below zero it opens down." to out
        add "מינימום ומקסימום" to out
    otherwise if which is 8:
        add "MAKE THE TWO Y VALUES MEET" to out
        add "where two graphs cross, their y values are equal. Set them equal and solve." to out
        add "מערכת משוואות" to out
    otherwise if which is 9:
        add "LEG SQUARED PLUS LEG SQUARED" to out
        add "leg squared + leg squared = hypotenuse squared." to out
        add "משפט פיתגורס" to out
    otherwise:
        add "SIDE TIMES SIDE" to out
        add "area is side times side. The diagonal is Pythagoras on the two sides." to out
        add "מלבן" to out
    thank you for checking

    give back out
thank you for defining


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Making a question
--
-- Every maker gives back the same five pieces of text, so that whoever asked does not have to
-- know which kind it was:
--
--   1  the question
--   2  the answer
--   3  the working, for when it goes wrong
--   4  which rule it belongs to
--   5  what the creature is called
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

please define a question of squares:
    remember k is a random whole number from 2 to 12
    remember square is k times k
    remember out is an empty list
    remember which is a random whole number from 1 to 3

    check if which is 1:
        add "Open the brackets:  (x + {k})(x - {k})\n    What is the number left at the end?" to out
        add the text of 0 minus square to out
        add "  a is x and b is {k}\n  (a + b)(a - b) = a squared - b squared\n  so it is x squared - {k} squared\n  and {k} squared is {square}\n  the number at the end is -{square}" to out
        add "1" to out
    otherwise if which is 2:
        add "Break into factors:  x squared - {square}\n    It comes out as (x - k)(x + k). What is k?" to out
        add the text of k to out
        add "  {square} is a square number\n  the square root of {square} is {k}\n  so x squared - {square} = (x - {k})(x + {k})\n  k is {k}" to out
        add "1" to out
    otherwise:
        add "Open the brackets:  (x + {k}) squared\n    What is the number in front of x?" to out
        add the text of 2 times k to out
        add "  (a + b) squared = a squared + 2ab + b squared\n  a is x and b is {k}\n  the middle piece is 2 times x times {k}\n  so the number in front of x is {2 times k}" to out
        add "2" to out
    thanks

    add "goblin" to out
    give back out
thank you for defining


please define a question of bottoms:
    remember k is a random whole number from 2 to 11
    remember m is a random whole number from 2 to 9
    remember out is an empty list
    remember which is a random whole number from 1 to 2

    check if which is 1:
        add "Here is a fraction:  {m times k} over (x - {k})\n    Which value of x is out of bounds?" to out
        add the text of k to out
        add "  the bottom can never be zero\n  so set the bottom to nothing:  x - {k} = 0\n  which gives x = {k}\n  that value is out of bounds" to out
    otherwise:
        add "Solve for x:  {m times k} over x = {m}" to out
        add the text of k to out
        add "  multiply both sides by x:  {m times k} = {m}x\n  divide both sides by {m}\n  x = {m times k} over {m} = {k}\n  and x is not 0, so it is allowed" to out
    thanks

    add "3" to out
    add "shade" to out
    give back out
thank you for defining


please define a question of parabolas:
    -- Built from two whole roots, so that every answer comes out whole.
    remember p is a random whole number from 1 to 6
    remember q is p plus a random whole number from 2 to 8
    remember middle is p plus q
    remember last is p times q
    remember out is an empty list
    remember which is a random whole number from 1 to 5

    check if which is 1:
        add "The parabola:  y = x squared - {middle}x + {last}\n    What is the x of the vertex?" to out
        add the text of middle over 2 to out
        add "  the rule is minus b over two a\n  a is 1 and b is -{middle}\n  so x = {middle} over 2\n  x = {middle over 2}" to out
        add "4" to out
    otherwise if which is 2:
        add "The parabola:  y = x squared - {middle}x + {last}\n    It crosses the x axis twice. What is the larger crossing?" to out
        add the text of q to out
        add "  make y nothing:  x squared - {middle}x + {last} = 0\n  it factors into (x - {p})(x - {q}) = 0\n  so x is {p} or x is {q}\n  the larger is {q}" to out
        add "5" to out
    otherwise if which is 3:
        add "The parabola:  y = x squared - {middle}x + {last}\n    Where does it cross the y axis?" to out
        add the text of last to out
        add "  the y axis is where x = 0\n  put 0 in:  0 - 0 + {last}\n  so it crosses at y = {last}" to out
        add "6" to out
    otherwise if which is 4:
        remember at is a random whole number from 0 to 8
        remember value is at times at minus middle times at plus last
        add "The parabola:  y = x squared - {middle}x + {last}\n    What is y when x is {at}?" to out
        add the text of value to out
        add "  put {at} in wherever x is\n  {at} squared is {at times at}\n  {middle} times {at} is {middle times at}\n  {at times at} - {middle times at} + {last} = {value}" to out
        add "4" to out
    otherwise:
        add "The parabola:  y = x squared - {middle}x + {last}\n    Type 1 if it smiles, or 2 if it frowns." to out
        add "1" to out
        add "  look at a, the number in front of x squared\n  here a is 1, which is above zero\n  a above zero opens upward, so it smiles\n  and its vertex is its lowest point" to out
        add "7" to out
    thanks

    add "ghost" to out
    give back out
thank you for defining


please define a question of meetings:
    -- A parabola and a line built to cross at two whole numbers.
    remember first is a random whole number from 1 to 5
    remember second is first plus a random whole number from 1 to 5
    remember slope is a random whole number from 1 to 4
    remember lift is a random whole number from 1 to 6

    remember b is slope minus first minus second
    remember c is lift plus first times second

    remember out is an empty list
    add "These two cross twice:\n      y = x squared + {b}x + {c}\n      y = {slope}x + {lift}\n    One crossing is at x = {first}. Where is the other?" to out
    add the text of second to out
    add "  where they cross, the two y values are equal\n  x squared + {b}x + {c} = {slope}x + {lift}\n  bring everything to one side and it factors\n  into (x - {first})(x - {second}) = 0\n  so the other crossing is x = {second}" to out
    add "8" to out
    add "wraith" to out
    give back out
thank you for defining


please define a question of corners:
    -- Right angled triangles with whole sides, so nothing comes out ragged.
    remember which is a random whole number from 1 to 6
    remember short is 3
    remember long is 4
    remember across is 5

    check if which is 2:
        change short to 6
        change long to 8
        change across to 10
    otherwise if which is 3:
        change short to 5
        change long to 12
        change across to 13
    otherwise if which is 4:
        change short to 8
        change long to 15
        change across to 17
    otherwise if which is 5:
        change short to 9
        change long to 12
        change across to 15
    otherwise if which is 6:
        change short to 7
        change long to 24
        change across to 25
    thanks

    remember out is an empty list
    remember ask is a random whole number from 1 to 2

    check if ask is 1:
        add "A right angled triangle has legs {short} and {long}.\n    How long is the hypotenuse?" to out
        add the text of across to out
        add "  leg squared + leg squared = hypotenuse squared\n  {short} squared is {short times short}\n  {long} squared is {long times long}\n  together that is {short times short plus long times long}\n  and the square root of {short times short plus long times long} is {across}" to out
    otherwise:
        add "A right angled triangle has a hypotenuse of {across}\n    and one leg of {short}. How long is the other leg?" to out
        add the text of long to out
        add "  leg squared + leg squared = hypotenuse squared\n  so leg squared = {across} squared - {short} squared\n  {across times across} - {short times short} = {across times across minus short times short}\n  and the square root of {across times across minus short times short} is {long}" to out
    thanks

    add "9" to out
    add "stone golem" to out
    give back out
thank you for defining


please define a question of rooms:
    remember wide is a random whole number from 3 to 20
    remember tall is a random whole number from 3 to 20
    remember area is wide times tall
    remember out is an empty list
    remember which is a random whole number from 1 to 2

    check if which is 1:
        add "A rectangle has an area of {area}.\n    One side is {wide}. How long is the other?" to out
        add the text of tall to out
        add "  area is side times side\n  so the other side is the area divided by the one you know\n  {area} over {wide}\n  which is {tall}" to out
        add "10" to out
    otherwise:
        add "A rectangle is {wide} by {tall}.\n    What is its perimeter?" to out
        add the text of 2 times (wide plus tall) to out
        add "  a rectangle has two of each side\n  {wide} + {tall} is {wide plus tall}\n  and twice that is {2 times (wide plus tall)}" to out
        add "10" to out
    thanks

    add "warden" to out
    give back out
thank you for defining


-- Which floor asks what.
please define a question for with a floor:
    check if floor is 1:
        give back a question of squares
    otherwise if floor is 2:
        give back a question of bottoms
    otherwise if floor is 3:
        give back a question of parabolas
    otherwise if floor is 4:
        give back a question of meetings
    otherwise if floor is 5:
        give back a question of corners
    otherwise if floor is 6:
        give back a question of rooms
    thanks
    -- The dragon takes from anywhere.
    give back a question for with a random whole number from 1 to 6
thank you for defining


please define the name of floor with a floor:
    check if floor is 1:
        give back "SHORT MULTIPLICATION AND FACTORS"
    otherwise if floor is 2:
        give back "EQUATIONS WITH BOTTOMS"
    otherwise if floor is 3:
        give back "PARABOLAS"
    otherwise if floor is 4:
        give back "WHERE GRAPHS MEET"
    otherwise if floor is 5:
        give back "PYTHAGORAS"
    otherwise if floor is 6:
        give back "RECTANGLES"
    thanks
    give back "THE DRAGON"
thank you for defining




please share the rule named and a question for and the name of floor
